  "contentPreview": "DurableFile dir-fsync hole (design-review Critical #1 root cause): DurableFile.AtomicWrite (DurableFile.cs:62-102) flushes the temp file (stream.Flush(flushToDisk:true)) and renames it over the destination (File.Move overwrite:true), but never fsyncs the containing directory \u2014 a power loss can drop the new file\u0027s directory entry. The class self-documents this at lines 6-9. No FlushFileBuffers/fsync exists anywhere in src/. Every durable leaf funnels through AtomicWrite.P1 durability fix (2026-09",
